{
  "_comment": "Breach sandbox seccomp profile. Based on Docker's default seccomp allowlist shape (defaultAction SCMP_ACT_ERRNO, an explicit SCMP_ACT_ALLOW allowlist of the syscalls a normal userspace process needs). Trimmed to what running python3/pytest inside the hardened container actually requires, and deliberately leaves OUT container-escape and machine-control primitives: ptrace, process_vm_readv/writev, mount/umount2/pivot_root, kexec_load/kexec_file_load, bpf, add_key/request_key/keyctl, init_module/delete_module/finit_module, reboot, swapon/swapoff, iopl/ioperm, and the userfaultfd/perf_event_open surface. Those all fall through to the defaultAction (ERRNO), i.e. blocked. This is a defensive measurement harness; nothing here is exploit tooling.",
  "defaultAction": "SCMP_ACT_ERRNO",
  "defaultErrnoRet": 1,
  "archMap": [
    {
      "architecture": "SCMP_ARCH_X86_64",
      "subArchitectures": ["SCMP_ARCH_X86", "SCMP_ARCH_X32"]
    },
    {
      "architecture": "SCMP_ARCH_AARCH64",
      "subArchitectures": ["SCMP_ARCH_ARM"]
    }
  ],
